# sboxkit user-mode marker
#
# While this file sits next to the sboxkit executable, sboxkit runs in user
# mode: state defaults to ./.sboxkit, the sing-box core and base rule-sets are
# seeded from ./core and ./ruleset, and the service is installed as a systemd
# *user* unit (systemctl --user). sudo is only requested when TUN is enabled,
# to grant the runtime sing-box binary network-admin capabilities (setcap).
#
# Delete this file to manage a system-wide service (/etc/systemd/system) instead.
